 "sparkline-table": "A compact metrics table with an inline SVG trend line per row, the latest value and the change over the series.",
 "avatar-stack": "Overlapping faces with a +N chip, each set in a ring of the surface colour. Hovering fans the stack out a little and tags the face with its name; arrow keys walk the faces, and the chip lists who is hidden. People who join or leave slide in and out.",
 "carousel": "A scroll-snap slider with previous/next buttons and dot indicators; arrow keys move between slides and the dots follow native scrolling.",
 "leaderboard": "Ranked rows with avatars, scores and a place-change arrow; the top three wear quiet mono medals, rows glide into their new order when the period changes, and your own row pins to the edge while it is out of view.",
 "timeline": "A vertical list of events on a 1 px rail: an icon in a small circle per event, the time, a title, an optional note and file chips. Runs of events with the same day sit under one day label, and a Show more fold opens the rest with a height animation; new events slide in at the top.",
 "month-calendar": "A month grid with roving-tabindex arrow-key navigation, a selected day, today marker and a dot under days that have events.",
 "file-manager": "A folder browser with a breadcrumb trail, a keyboard-navigable listbox (arrows, Enter to open, Backspace to go up) and name, size and modified columns, folders first.",
 "sortable-list": "A list you reorder by dragging a row's grip, or from the keyboard: Space lifts the row, the arrows carry it, Space drops it and Escape puts it back, while a live region reads out each new position. The other rows reflow with a spring; an optional round × removes a row.",
 "cohort-table": "A retention heatmap where each row is a cohort and each column a period; cell tint scales with the retained share.",
 "org-chart": "A top-down tree of people; a pure layout places each node (leaves in order, parents centred over their children) and SVG elbow connectors join them.",
 "gantt-chart": "A timeline of tasks as bars across a date range, with week gridlines, a month header and a vertical line for today.",
 "cycle-card": "A sprint or cycle summary with its date range, a status chip, days left, a stacked progress bar of completed, started and remaining scope, and counts.",
 "gantt-row": "One task line of a Gantt chart, a label beside a track holding a bar positioned by date within the visible range, with optional progress fill.",
 "audio-player": "A player for voice notes, call recordings and AI voice replies: a 48 px pill for message threads, or a card with the recording's name, source and date. Click or drag the waveform to seek and the played part fills in as it plays; the card adds 10 s skips, elapsed and remaining times, a 1× / 1.5× / 2× chip and an optional transcript row. Loading and error swap the play button's glyph and dim the controls, with Retry. It plays a real file from src, or runs on a timer for previews.",
 "rolling-number": "A number whose changed digits roll to their new values one after another, left to right, on tabular figures so the width never jumps, with a chip for the change: up in green and down in red, or the other way round for costs. The wheels turn the way the number moved and keep going past 9, a roll cut short carries on from where it is, and the final value is read out once. Two sizes, and any currency or unit through format.",
 "integration-card": "A connectable service tile with icon, name, description and a connect/disconnect button that shows a pending state while the async handler runs.",
 "swipe-row": "A list row that slides left on drag to reveal action buttons; it snaps open or closed by distance and velocity, and Arrow keys or Escape do the same from the keyboard.",
